    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. When we look at the data for those specific communities in District 2, there's also some mention of traditional ways of handling hygiene or communal food preparation that might differ from Western standards. For the sake of the accuracy of the model, should we be looking at whether these specific cultural/ethnic practices or traditional hygiene behaviors might actually be a primary driver of the spread, or is it strictly just the density and social structure?",
